// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - HelpIDF 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P995289774" "IDF Support"
// DetailString :
"P1314130529" "You agreed to help the IDF by rescuing Commander Gerard from Vanguard custody. You could always go back on your word, but it would mean dealing with the IDF down the line."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DeanMacArthur 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3625616018" "Dean MacArthur's Oath"
// DetailString :
"P1583226980" "Dean MacArthur swore that he would help you out and keep an eye out on this mysterious man who seems to be tracking your movements."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SavedIDF 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P251321263" "Commander Gerard Saved"
// DetailString :
"P3893174099" "You stayed true to your word and saved Commander Gerard. This should keep the remaining IDF from breathing down your back."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Subjugator 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2108811281" "Codename Subjugator 5"
// DetailString :
"P2425773659" "Transmuter told you that Vanguard has a powerful Subjugator deep within the prison. The Subjugators were failed seer experiments who had sickly growths shooting from their heads. Normally, they're incredibly powerful and insane. However, Subjugator 5 is different. She is able to control herself, to an extent, and is also powerful.<br><br>Perhaps if you could free her from Vanguard you could gain yet another member of your team."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PraetorBerry 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1315915798" "Praetor Berry's Fate"
// DetailString :
"P3117486557" "Bobcat explained to you what happened to Praetor Berry, AKA Neuron, AKA Bobcat's ex-boyfriend. Berry and Bobcat were teleported to safety after Vanguard's attack on Neutropolis.<br><br>The two hid in the Neutropolis until Emperor Cole was defeated and Hamidon attacked.<br><br>Berry tried to use Bobcat as bait for the Hamidon while he got away, but Bobcat saw through Berry's plan. In a fit of passionate rage, Bobcat killed Praetor Berry, then was captured by the Vanguard. The scientists in Vanguard used some sort of serum to prevent Bobcat from flying into a rage, leaving her to be nothing more than a socialite."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL6_7_i24_Arc_One 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1593110218" "Transmuter's Watch"
// tDetailString :
"P1334690801" "Transmuter gave you his favorite watch in appreciation for breaking him free of the Vanguard prison. It reminds you of an experience you call...<br><br><b>Criminals of War</b><br><br>You and Mr. G had a plan - free several prisoners of war that Vanguard had captured, then make the prisoners work for you.<br><br>You helped a former Vanguard general out of a bind and gained his aid in gaining access to the Vanguard prison.<br><br>You then assaulted the Vanguard prison, freeing Transmuter, Splice, Bobcat, and Subjugator 5.<br><br>Before you could do anything with them, Wu Yin announced a bounty on your head, knowing that you had freed all of these prisoners.<br><br>It would appear Wu Yin desperately wants you put down - you'll just have to show him what you and your new team can actually do."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - FlashbackLeft 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Computer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P980095992" "<color orange>You access Vanguard's remote computer and tap into one of the cameras on the roof. You see General Alito and some of his loyalists are cornered by several Vanguard soldiers and their heavy assault suits.<br><br>You could wait until the groups fight each other, then swoop in and clean up the mess, or you could jump in before the fighting begins to aid Alito and his men.<br><br><color orange>Aiding Alito before the fighting begins will be very difficult, especially if you're going to do it alone.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1367882209" "(Go up and help Alito)"
// Answer Text :
"P921192691" "(Wait for the fight to be over)"
// Page GoUp Text :
"P856364347" ""
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page CutsceneStart Text :
"P2777611791" "<color orange>You wait a few minutes and watch General Alito and his men fight against Vanguard's forces. Alito and his men take out a good number of Vanguard before they're cornered.<br><br>Now it's your turn to go up top and handle things.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - General 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Help Text :
"P1100616345" "{HeroName}, I am in your debt for your help. There would've been a day where I would have attacked you, but now my allies are in short supply.<br><br>You must want me for something, otherwise you would have just attacked me by now."
// Answer Text :
"P3078473158" "(Explain the situation to Alito)"
// Page Explain Text :
"P1141455947" "That is something I could easily help you with. If I know Vanguard, they will have brought the prisoners to one of their sea bases over in the pacific.<br><br>It's well guarded from unknown air or submarine access. You'll need to commandeer a <color yellow>Vanguard helicopter</color> in order to get there. If you can get me a helicopter and the codes to pilot it, I can fly you straight to the base. I'll use some old authorization codes to get us a landing permit to the base.<br><br>From what I can tell, Vanguard should have a helicopter somewhere in St. Martial; the pursuers who were after me were talking about tracking down some IDF who are holed up in a Rikti base."
// Answer Text :
"P3006176707" "Alright, Alito, you've got a deal."
// Page NoHelp Text :
"P3749369675" ""{HeroName}, thank you for your help. If only you had arrived sooner, perhaps the battle would have gone smoother, but I will not be picky about my lucky chances.<br><br>I could use an ally or two in the Isles, as you can see. I'm assuming you need me for something, or else you would've attacked me by now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - VanguardLeader 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2338449183" "<color orange>You use your unique abilities to extract the codes that General Alito needs to pilot the Vanguard helicopter. Now that you have the codes, you don't necessarily need this man any longer.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1241125825" "(Kill the operative)"
// Answer Text :
"P594480677" "(Leave him for General Alito to deal with)"
// Page KillLeader Text :
"P3447255354" "This world is full of super villains. They want to do evil things like take over the world."
// Page General Text :
"P1407234927" "I think it's going to rain tomorrow."
// Answer Text :
"P1443913718" "Try again."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - VanguardLeaderPeaceful 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Answer Text :
"P2649146381" "(Leave him for the IDF)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - IDFCommander 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page PowersPraetoria Text :
"P3411155270" "{HeroName}. I remember you <i>quite</i> well. You were one of those power-hungry freaks from Praetoria, always trying to do everything for yourself. Weren't you the one to defeat the first Olympian Guard clone?<br><br>I have <i>no</i> respect for you, so if you want anything, you can just forget about it. Leave now, and perhaps we won't <i>kill</i> you."
// Answer Text :
"P3420173920" "That was an unwise choice, Commander. (Attack!)"
// Page ResponsibilityPraetoria Text :
"P434687144" "I remember you... {HeroName}, you were the one who helped protect Anti-Matter's reactor against Arachnos! I thought you were a good person... But now look at you. You're dwelling the Isles? You have stained your good reputation from Praetoria!<br><br>I cannot trust you, not when you've fallen so far. Leave now, and I won't have my troops open fire on you. But if you stay, then I will be forced to put you down."
// Answer Text :
"P2156756722" "Then there's only one option. (Attack!)"
// Page Primal Text :
"P4055684753" "You... what is it that you want from me? You're not here with Vanguard to try to bring us in, or else you'd have done it already.<br><br>My men and I are just trying to establish a new base here while waiting for orders from the others who escaped."
// Answer Text :
"P2781671010" "I'm not going to bother with words! (Attack!)"
// Answer Text :
"P3896966273" "I'm here to make you an offer, to join my team."
// Answer Text :
"P2519593769" "I'm here for the Vanguard operative that you have."
// Page General Text :
"P2366501000" "No, {HeroName}, I serve Praetoria, I serve Emperor Cole, even in his moment of darkness!<br><Br>I would never betray the oath that I have sworn."
// Answer Text :
"P417690931" "Alright, then we'll do this the hard way! (Attack!)"
// Answer Text :
"P1392989975" "Fair enough. I want the Vanguard operative in your custody."
// Page Leader Text :
"P2582114410" "We need the operative for leverage, {HeroName}. Then again... if you're here, it must mean you've taken out the Vanguard topside. Very well, I'll make you a deal.<br><br>We'll hand the operative over to you on the condition that you help free one of our own, Commander Gerard, from the Vanguard prison he is being held in. I must warn you, however. If you make this deal and break it, we <i>will</i> track you down. Our vengeance will be swift and powerful.<br><br><color orange>You can always promise to help the IDF out and just simply not rescue the commander. Perhaps it would even be better. The people in the Isles need to know you're not one to be crossed!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1956189850" "Alright, I'll recover your commander from the Vanguard."
// Answer Text :
"P1126680802" "No deal, I'm taking the operative! (Attack!)"
// Page Agree Text :
"P972524947" "Excellent. You can find the operative in the back. Take what you need from him. We'll be expecting Commander Gerard back in our custody soon, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P964984125" "You have my word."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Dmac 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1376567421" "YO! {HeroName}! What up! It's been a while, {Hero.gender=male man|my beautiful flower}! I bet you're wondering, 'Dean, what is someone so cool like you doing calling me out of the blue?'<br><br>Wonder no more! So, check it. I dunno who it is, but some guy has been keeping tabs on your movements. I think he's got a plan to go after you.<br><br>Now, you and me, we're like, thick and thin, right? I mean, {Hero.gender=male we're bros, right?|you could cut the romantic tension between us with a knife!} So I'm thinkin' this.<br><br>I'll keep an ear to the ground, try to see if someone is gonna mess with you. If I find anything out, I'll let you know, 'cause that's what a guy like D-Mac does!"
// Answer Text :
"P3215130505" "... Right, thanks Dean."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MrGMission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page IDFAttack Text :
"P3437407665" "Ah, {HeroName}. As you can see, everyone has been gathered. It's a shame that Bobcat can no longer be an able fighter, but she will do well to help find you information. She will have to, at least. The catgirl has become far too lazy to be a capable fighter. I will, of course, look into ways of fixing that.<br><br>We're still in control of Vanguard's helicopter; this will allow us to do whatever we wish in the future."
// Answer Text :
"P3114795522" "Excellent. Now, on to our first plan..."
// Page NormalAfterIDFAttack Text :
"P1500367031" "... Well, it appears you still had some unfinished business. Very unfinished."
// Answer Text :
"P3177230240" "Let's get back to the main point."
// Page MainDialog Text :
"P4004558035" "There are several paths that I would suggest we take with our plans. Subjugator 5, of course, is a major asset. The power stored within that... <i>thing</i> could be devastating, when directed at the right target. I believe it's just a matter of finding <i>who</i> who go after first with it."
// Answer Text :
"P350864113" "You're my information man. Get me a list of targets."
// Page Bobcat Text :
"P3722424029" "<img align=left src=costume:Model_Bobcat_GR_NoRing width=128 height=128>Hey! There's something on the communicator here. They're talking about us. I knew it was a good idea to hang around all of you!"
// Answer Text :
"P1701357831" "What? (Look at the communicator)"
// Page NormalAfterCutsceneDean Text :
"P4260193091" "It seems you have more friends than I knew of, {HeroName}. This Dean MacArthur proved useful in stopping Wu Yin from revealing more about us.<br><br>Myself and the others will work on a proper plan of attack for you. We should have something together in very little time, and we will be able to provide you the support necessary to <i>stomp out</i> Mr. Yin."
// Answer Text :
"P4131309922" "Good to hear, Mr. G."
// Page NormalAfterCutscene Text :
"P3737447590" "This is troubling, {HeroName}, very troubling. Our presence is now publically known. I should have guessed that Wu Yin would try something like this.<br><br>Myself and the others will work on a proper plan of attack for you. We should have something together in very little time, and we will be able to provide you the support necessary to <i>stomp out</i> Mr. Yin."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MrGDoor 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3154508904" "Shall we get started, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P3699372019" "(Enter mission)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3526934882" "I shall lay out the scenario for you, {HeroName}. Vanguard has captured several people who are war criminals. There are some very... <i>big</i> names on that list, namely <color yellow>Praetor Duncan</color> and <color yellow>Emperor Cole</color>, very big names. Both will be going on trial for their crimes. It's all very... old fashioned, if you ask me. Now, I would suggest that you do not bother with them; Cole would never work with you, and Duncan is too much of a little manipulator to trust, quite the manipulator.<br><br>Instead, I suggest we break out those who would be in your debt and be quite easy to control. I have it on good authority that <color yellow>Bobcat, Transmuter, and Splice</color> were all captured.<br><br>Bobcat is a drama queen, but she... <i>can</i> be a good combatant. Transmuter has experience from the Hamidon wars, and if his powers could be returned to him, he would be a valuable ally. Splice is technological mastermind and has the moral compass of a brick, just like a brick.<br><br>We would all make quite a good team to aid you, quite a good team."
// AcceptString :
"P1641587913" "Alright. I need a way to recover all of them."
// SendOffString :
"P2250784981" "Yes, exactly, I have done some research and have recovered just what you need. Vanguard is keeping these prisoners in one of their secure locations, much more secure than they have previously, due to some... issues with someone breaking out a prisoner. We would need someone on the inside, someone who knows where their prisoners are located.<br><br>There is a man, his name is <color yellow>General Alito</color>. He was a member of Vanguard who went rogue during their Rikti operation. He's broken out of their custody and is now on the run in St. Martial. Quite coincidental, almost providential.<br><br>If you can assist him, I'm sure you could persuade the man to help you in your plan.<br><br>Here is his last known location. There are a few Vanguard who have been ordered to pursue Alito, the others are acting as guards. You'll have to take out the pursuers and ensure that they have nothing that can directly track Alito. I will be available, should you need any more advice."
// TaskTitle :
"P2907695024" "<color deepskyblue>Criminals of War</color>"

